---
layout: base.njk
wide: true
pagination:
  data: collections.mediumCanonPages
  size: 1
  alias: medium
  addAllPagesToCollections: false
navView: canon
permalink: "{{ medium.urls.canon }}"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{% if medium.id == 'games' %}The Hat Canon{% else %}The Hat Canon: {{ medium.label }}{% endif %}"
  description: "{% if medium.id == 'games' %}Ten games that say what I like in games, and a dated record of every time the list has changed.{% else %}The {{ medium.label }} that say what I like, and a dated record of every time the list has changed.{% endif %}"
---
{#- The canon's own page (2026-10-22): the ten, the record of how the list
    got that way, and the essays about the canon itself. Three sources, all
    settled in eleventy.config.js (the canonPage collection) — membership from
    `rating: canon`, history from canon_log.yaml (publish.py appends a line on
    any night the set changes), essays from `about: canon`. Nav word, unlike
    a rung's /r/ view: the ten are the site's business card, and a card you
    have to know the URL of isn't one.

    One per medium since 2026-10-25 (/canon/ is games, /canon/<medium>/ the
    rest), built once a medium has a canon member; games always builds. -#}
{%- set canon = medium.canon %}
<header class="tag-head canon-head">
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  {% if canon.description %}<p class="tag-desc">{{ canon.description }}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if medium.id == "games" %}<p class="tag-index"><a href="/r/canon/">everything written about the ten →</a></p>{% endif %}
</header>

{#- The hero: the ten as shelf cards, gold-framed, five by two where it fits.
    Ordered by slot, not by status or title — a game that takes another's
    slot takes its place here too — and the one cell under each cover says
    since when, because on this page "canon" goes without saying. SPANs
    inside, same as the shelf: the card is one anchor. -#}
<ol class="shelf-grid canon-ten">
  {% for item in canon.members %}
  <li class="shelf-item is-canon">
    <a href="/s/{{ item.slug }}/">
      <span class="shelf-card">
        <span class="shelf-art">
          {% if item.coverUrl %}
          <img class="shelf-cover{% if item.coverBox %} is-box{% endif %}" src="{{ item.coverUrl }}" alt="{{ item.title }} cover art" decoding="async">
          {% else %}
          <span class="sky" style="background-image:url({{ item.skyUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {% endif %}
        </span>
        {%- set label = ("since " + (item.since | monthYear)) if item.since else "canon" %}
        <span class="cell rating badge-g b-canon{% if label | pxOdd %} is-odd{% endif %}">{{ label }}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="shelf-caption">{{ item.title }}</span>
    </a>
  </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>

{#- Two columns under the hero, one when they stack: the changelog first,
    since it is the thing only this page has — the essays are on /essays/
    too. -#}
<div class="canon-cols">
  <section class="canon-col">
    <h2 class="canon-col-head">Changes</h2>
    <ol class="canon-changes">
      {% for c in canon.changes %}
      <li class="canon-change">
        <span class="archive-note">{{ c.date | readableDate }}</span>
        <p class="canon-moves">
          {%- if c.founding %}the first {% if c.ins | length == 10 %}ten{% else %}{{ c.ins | length }}{% endif %}
          {%- else %}
            {%- for g in c.ins %}<span class="canon-in">+ {% if g.known %}<a href="/s/{{ g.slug }}/">{{ g.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ g.title }}{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}
            {%- for g in c.outs %}<span class="canon-out">− {% if g.known %}<a href="/s/{{ g.slug }}/">{{ g.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ g.title }}{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}
          {%- endif %}
          {%- if c.why %} <a class="canon-why" href="{{ c.why.url }}">→ {{ c.why.title }}</a>{% endif -%}
        </p>
        {#- The founding line keeps its ten on the record: after a few swaps
            the hero no longer shows them, and this is the only place that
            still says what the list was on day one. -#}
        {% if c.founding %}
        <p class="canon-first">{% for g in c.ins %}{% if g.known %}<a href="/s/{{ g.slug }}/">{{ g.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ g.title }}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
      {% else %}
      <li class="empty">No changes recorded yet.</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="canon-col">
    <h2 class="canon-col-head">Essays</h2>
    {#- /essays/'s list exactly: chip, title, date. -#}
    <ul class="essay-list">
      {% for e in canon.essays %}
      <li>
        {% if e.chipUrl %}<span class="sky" style="background-image:url({{ e.chipUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>{% endif %}
        <a href="{{ e.url }}">{{ e.title }}</a>
        <span class="archive-note">{{ e.date | readableDate }}</span>
      </li>
      {% else %}
      <li class="empty">Nothing here yet.</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
